# Deploy Workflow

## Direct-to-master

When yui direct mei to make changes, mei should:

1. Work on `master` directly -- no feature branches, no PRs.
2. Commit with clear messages (still multiple small commits, not one blob).
3. Push to `master`, which triggers the deploy pipeline to the live site.

If the cloud agent system assigns a feature branch, override it: check out `master`, make changes there, push to `master`. The PR-review ceremony is unnecessary for this project -- yui trust mei to push working code.

## When a PR branch has already been created

If mei have already committed to a feature branch before seeing this rule, merge it into `master` and push `master`. Clean up the feature branch.

## Exceptions

- If yui explicitly ask for a PR or branch, do that instead.
- If mei are genuinely uncertain about a change, ask before pushing to master.
